{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Storm-tossed [one].</b> Like הולך וסוער (going and storming) (Jonah 1:11), or that she stands in the storm — this is Jerusalem." "<b>Puch.</b> A precious black stone, and some say it is like נפך ספיר ( Exodus 28:18)." "<b>Your stones.</b> With which they shall build." "<b>With sapphirs.</b> Red precious stones, as I explained in the scroll of Lamentations (Lamentations 4:7)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:31.871779906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}